Subject: [PATCH] opengles: present quarter turns in LVGL's direction on DRM/EGL

lv_opengles_render_display() fills its vertex table a quarter turn clockwise,
while lv_display_rotate_point() maps pointer input counter-clockwise. On the
DRM/EGL path with software rendering, which presents through
lv_opengles_texture_present_display() with v_flip=false and scans the render
target's row 0 out at the panel's physical top, that leaves touch reversed on
both axes of a GPU-rotated display, so the two quarter turns trade places.

The SDL-EGL (lv_sdl_egl.c) and Wayland (lv_wayland_backend_egl.c) paths reach
the same function through lv_opengles_texture_render_display(): with software
rendering they pass v_flip=false as DRM does, and with LV_USE_DRAW_OPENGLES
they pass v_flip=true, where the correct direction is the opposite one. Only
the DRM software path is verified; a build presenting through either of the
others needs the swap checked, and made conditional on the caller if it is
wrong there.

diff --git a/src/drivers/opengles/lv_opengles_driver.c b/src/drivers/opengles/lv_opengles_driver.c
index 24b164191..d373f4347 100644
--- a/src/drivers/opengles/lv_opengles_driver.c
+++ b/src/drivers/opengles/lv_opengles_driver.c
@@ -351,6 +351,10 @@ void lv_opengles_render_display(lv_display_t * display, const lv_opengles_render
     GL_CALL(glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, texture));
 
     lv_display_rotation_t rotation = lv_display_get_rotation(display);
+    /*LVGL turns a quarter turn counter-clockwise (lv_display_rotate_point() maps pointer input
+     *that way), and the vertex table turns the other way, so the two quarter turns trade places*/
+    if(rotation == LV_DISPLAY_ROTATION_90) rotation = LV_DISPLAY_ROTATION_270;
+    else if(rotation == LV_DISPLAY_ROTATION_270) rotation = LV_DISPLAY_ROTATION_90;
     bool h_flip = params->h_flip;
     bool v_flip = params->v_flip;
 
